  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sealed Letter at Dusk",
    "overview": "The phone screen is the envelope, edge to edge: ivory paper whose florals exist only as blind-embossed relief, closed with a cream wax seal stamped with a gold-leaf monogram. Breaking the seal is the single orchestrated moment of the page. Light comes before movement: the seal glows, gold dust lifts off it, the flaps part on amber light, a warm bloom washes the screen, and a carved ganch (alabaster) arch settles in with Samarkand's domes and minarets dissolving into gold haze behind the couple's names.\n\nAfter the opening the page is calm and devotional: one centred phone-width column on ganch ivory, sepia ink, gilt hairlines, pointed-arch panels whose gold outline draws itself in view. Ornament is relief and light, not colour. Every scene is drawn in code (SVG, CSS, one canvas); there are no photographs, paintings or people.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Full-bleed envelope as the first viewport; the seal is the only control.",
      "Paper-on-paper relief: motifs carry the paper's own tone, shaped by a light/shadow filter.",
      "Gold is a material (leaf, gilt edge, coin), rendered as gradients from deep antique to pale champagne, never as a flat accent fill.",
      "Sepia ink throughout; no black anywhere a guest can see.",
      "Two faces: Corinthia script for names and spoken greetings, Bodoni Moda for everything set.",
      "Slow exponential ease-out; one choreographed sequence, then only ambient motion (lantern swing, flicker, breathing glow)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Sepia Rule",
        "body": "Ink is brown, never black. Black (`#000`, `rgba(0,0,0,.5)`) appears only as an alpha mask inside relief filters, where it is never painted.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Is Not Paint Rule",
        "body": "Amber and the white-gold radial blooms describe light sources (seal, lanterns, envelope interior, sun disc). They never fill a card, a button or text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Spoken Script Rule",
        "body": "Corinthia sets only names and words a person would say or sign. Instructions, data and headings are Bodoni Moda.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Line Rule",
        "body": "The sealed envelope carries exactly one line of text, an italic instruction under the seal. Nothing else is printed on the paper.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Relief Not Ink Rule",
        "body": "Embossed motifs (envelope florals, section sprays, ganch carving) are drawn as alpha shapes and turned into light and shadow by a filter; they always end up the tone of the surface they are carved into.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do render gold as a gradient material with a highlight and a darker edge (deep antique to pale champagne), not as a flat fill.",
      "Do keep every motif paper-on-paper: draw alpha shapes and let the relief filter turn them into light and shadow.",
      "Do time motion with the slow ease-out (`cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`) and bring light in before movement.",
      "Do derive arches from the shared pointed-arch path so the hero, panels and map read as one architecture.",
      "Do keep fixed controls aligned to the 480px column and clear of safe-area insets.",
      "Do honour reduced motion with the shortened flap opening and static ornaments."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't print colour ornament on the envelope; it carries only relief, the seal and one italic line.",
      "Don't use black ink or neutral grey anywhere visible; text is sepia.",
      "Don't add a second orchestrated moment after the opening; later motion stays ambient or reveal-on-view.",
      "Don't set instructions, data or headings in the script face.",
      "Don't add photographs, paintings or figures to the scene; it is architecture, light and ornament drawn in code.",
      "Don't let a later template borrow these tokens, the seal or the arch; it shares only the showcase shell."
    ]
  }
}